  HOW TO READ THIS:
  * Both arms were fitted AFTER the 2026-08-25f seasonal-NEP isotope fix, so
    `streams` is the decomposition of that par_mode under the CURRENT
    objective and every row should reproduce. A non-empty list above is a
    REGRESSION or a new objective change -- not a known backlog.
  * THE ARMS ARE LIKE-FOR-LIKE HERE, unlike the pre-fix N-vs-D pair this file
    used to run: both were fitted in the same 3-arm refit on the same
    objective. What is NOT comparable is their STORED logpost -- `pin90`
    carries a near-delta prior on `fert_k` worth +11.6698, so its -1544.50
    is -1556.17 on the free scale, 11.56 BELOW the canonical mode. Compare
    the GATES below, not the logposts.
  * The pre-fix arms N and D are quarantined under
    output/quarantine/20260825_seas_isotope_rectification/ and are NOT
    comparable with anything here; ccx_mode_file() refuses them by name.

