=== GATE 5 FOLLOW-UP: tau_ex PROFILE at the shipped mode (others FROZEN) ===
  observed NH->SH bomb lag 1.34 yr; the mode's tau_ex is 1.159 yr
   tau_ex  bomb lag     co2_grad    d13c_grad   total logL
    0.600      0.51       -424.0        -70.5      -2855.7
    0.800      0.88       -178.4         35.4      -2040.7
    1.159      0.97         -5.2        105.9      -1622.3
    1.400      1.01        -76.3         73.8      -1775.4
    2.000      1.11       -878.1       -250.8      -3214.1
    3.000      1.91      -4061.1      -1429.3      -8366.0

  THE TWO OBSERVABLES DISAGREE, AND THE GRADIENT WINS BY THREE ORDERS OF
  MAGNITUDE. The bomb lag rises monotonically with tau_ex and needs roughly
  2.3 yr to reach the observed 1.34; both gradient streams sit at a sharp
  INTERIOR optimum at the mode's 1.159 and fall away steeply on both sides.
  So gate 5's lag miss is a FORCED residual, not an overlooked one -- the
  model cannot satisfy both interhemispheric constraints with one tau_ex,
  which makes this a STRUCTURAL finding about the two-box exchange rather
  than a parameter that has not been tried.

==========================================================================
THE GATE LEDGER -- source class, bound, and whether the gate has POWER
==========================================================================

GATE 4 -- airborne fraction 1959-2024
  class : OBSERVATION
  source: GCB 2025
  bound : ORDERING, no threshold (2026-09-02): 
            sd(model decadal AF) >= sd(GCB decadal AF). The gate's own 
            stated claim is 'must not be SMOOTHER than this', and an 
            ordering gets no threshold. ⚠ The AF LEVEL stays UNBOUNDED 
            on purpose -- see POWER.
  scored: YES (CO2 growth is fitted; emissions are inputs)
  POWER : ~NONE on the LEVEL -- near-algebraic in quantities the fit 
            already matches, so a bound there would test the optimiser. 
            REAL on the VARIABILITY: nothing in the objective asks the 
            decadal AF to vary, and the model is currently too smooth.

GATE 5 -- bomb 14C peak, hemispheric lag, e-fold
  class : OBSERVATION
  source: Hua et al. 2022, hemispheric aggregate
  bound : TWO KINDS (2026-09-02). ORDERINGS, no threshold: 
            SH peaks AFTER NH, NH peak HIGHER than SH -- the bomb source 
            was northern. DISTRIBUTIONAL: |z| <= DG_G5_NSD on peak times 
            and lag, against a sigma DERIVED by leave-one-zone-out on the 
            observed aggregate (Hua publishes none). ⚠ That sigma is the 
            aggregate's sensitivity to its own zonal composition, not a 
            measurement error, and rests on few draws.
  scored: STREAM yes, FUNCTIONAL no (likelihood scores levels)
  POWER : MODERATE, and the best-sourced gate here: a different 
            functional of a scored stream. It now HAS a bound.

GATE 7 -- land / ocean sinks 2015-2023
  class : OBSERVATION + MODEL
  source: GCB 2025. ⚠ MIXED: the ocean sink is a product of ocean 
            biogeochemistry MODELS and the land sink is a RESIDUAL of the 
            budget, so this is not a clean observation.
  bound : |z| <= DG_G7_NSD (2 since 2026-09-02), against the 
            OBJECTIVE'S OWN sigmas: land 1.50 = LIK_GCB_LAND_SD x 
            LIK_LAND_SINK_INFLATE, ocean 0.40 uninflated. ⚠ Until 
            2026-09-02 it judged land at 0.50, three times stricter than 
            the fit, which is where its standing FAIL came from.
  scored: YES -- gcb_land_sink and gcb_ocean_sink are BOTH fitted
  POWER : STILL NONE out-of-sample -- same streams, same data, and 
            aligning the sigma does not change that. What it now tests is 
            whether the optimiser did its job, which is worth stating and 
            is not worth chasing in a refit.

GATE Q -- air-sea d13C disequilibrium, 1995
  class : OBSERVATION
  source: Quay et al. 2003 (0.60 +- 0.10 permil)
  bound : n_sd <= DG_Q_NSD, a distributional claim on the stated sigma
  scored: NO -- ocean d13C is scored as a GRADIENT; d13c_level_* are atmospheric
  POWER : REAL, AND THE ONLY ONE. Nothing constrains absolute 
            surface-ocean d13C, which is why it caught a 6.4-sigma 
            wrong-sign error that no stream had ever objected to.

GATE G -- ocean mixed-layer DIC level at the GLODAP epoch
  class : OBSERVATION
  source: GLODAPv2.2023, doi:10.25921/z7hc-v261; 
            Lauvset et al. 2024 ESSD 16:2047. Volume-weighted on the 
            MODEL's own top layer, at the bottles' own mean year.
  bound : |z| <= DG_GD_NSD on the SURFACE LEVEL only. ⚠ The column 
            INVENTORY is reported and NOT bounded: the pump's export was 
            solved to hold the OBSERVED gradient, so an inventory gate 
            would partly read back what built it.
  scored: NO -- the three ocean rows are GRADIENTS with fitted 
            offsets, d14c_deep_ocean is Delta14C, gcb_ocean_sink is a FLUX. 
            Nothing that set the model's surface DIC saw this number.
  POWER : REAL and OUT-OF-SAMPLE, and it LOCALISES: the surface 
            Revelle factor is a function of surface DIC and alkalinity, so 
            a level that is right bounds gate 12a's ocean-capacity defect 
            AWAY from the surface carbonate state. ⚠ Its sigma borrows the 
            ABYSSAL n_eff = 20, which is conservative at the surface.

GATE 12/12b -- Joos IRF: integrated pulse response, and the tail
  class : MODEL
  source: Joos et al. 2013 multi-model mean, vintage 2013. 
            ⚠ LAST-RESORT source class: a threshold from another model. 
            Named here rather than discovered. 12b's band is CONSTRUCTED 
            (Joos publishes no 5-95 % at TH 300) and says so.
  bound : 12a: Joos published 5-95 %. 12b: constructed band, stated.
  scored: NO -- the IRF is not a stream
  POWER : REAL, and 12b carries its OWN in-run mutation test.

  GATE 7's sigmas, computed not quoted: it JUDGES at land 1.50 / ocean 0.40
    (= LIK_GCB_LAND_SD 0.50 x LIK_LAND_SINK_INFLATE 3.0, and the ocean
    UNINFLATED at 0.40 -- the objective's own asymmetry). GCB's STATED
    sigmas, which the report prints beside the target, are 0.50 / 0.40.
  The three distributional gates now share one strictness: DG_G5_NSD 2,
    DG_G7_NSD 2, DG_Q_NSD 2.
  ⚠ STILL NO LAW-DERIVED GATE. GATE G (2026-09-02) is OBSERVATIONAL; it
    puts an observation ON the surface carbonate state, which narrows the
    hole without closing it. Candidates, none built: carbonate / Revelle
    consistency, and Henry's-law solubility.

